iterations.reply:
The compile error came from two types that the world does not name directly. `LlmError` and `AgentResponse` live under `crate::aap::caps::types::`, so the fix is to import them there.

I did not add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The graph definition doesn't declare that capability yet, so importing it would give this node outbound network access the contract doesn't grant. The fetch would also send the customer's question text to an external host in a URL query string. If the platform team has approved this, the graph and capability declaration should change first, and I can add the call once it does.

